From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Date: Wed, 1 Jan 2025 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: dts: k230: describe the watchdog as wdt0 at 375 kHz

The K230 watchdog that the system uses is wdt0 at 0x91106000 on PLIC
source 107. Rewrite the wdt1@91106800 node in place as
watchdog0: wdt0@91106000 rather than adding a second node: with two
enabled snps,dw-wdt instances both register with the watchdog core and
/dev/watchdog binds to whichever probes first.

wdt0 is clocked from osc24m through a 1..64 divider, and nothing in
Linux programs that divider unless the device tree asks for a rate.
assigned-clocks and assigned-clock-rates = <375000> make the k230
composite clock select div = 64 before dw_wdt_probe() reads the rate.

At 375 kHz the DesignWare timeout periods (2^(16+i) counts) give the
whole-second grid

  0 0 0 1 2 5 11 22 44 89 178 357 715 1431 2863 5726

so an 89 s timeout is period i=9 (2^25 / 375000 = 89.478 s), and with
the pre-timeout armed dw_wdt grants a pre-timeout of 89 s and a timeout
of 178 s.

The PLIC uses two interrupt cells and the soc node supplies the
interrupt parent, so the interrupt is <107 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>; dw_wdt
requests IRQF_TRIGGER_RISING, which overrides the type at request time.
The node has no resets property, so dw_wdt_stop() leaves
WDOG_HW_RUNNING set.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 arch/riscv/boot/dts/canaan/k230.dtsi | 10 ++++++----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/canaan/k230.dtsi b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/canaan/k230.dtsi
index 051289e0c..50a17fb02 100644
--- a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/canaan/k230.dtsi
+++ b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/canaan/k230.dtsi
@@ -426,11 +426,13 @@ i2c4: i2c@91409000 {
 			status = "disabled";
 		};
 
-		watchdog1: wdt1@91106800 {
+		watchdog0: wdt0@91106000 {
 			compatible = "snps,dw-wdt";
-			reg = <0x0 0x91106800 0x0 0x800>;
-			interrupts = <108 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
-			clocks = <&wdt1>;
+			reg = <0x0 0x91106000 0x0 0x800>;
+			interrupts = <107 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			clocks = <&wdt0>;
+			assigned-clocks = <&wdt0>;
+			assigned-clock-rates = <375000>;
 		};
 
 		adc: adc@9140d000 {
